RISC-V mathvec ABI framework
============================

This directory carries the downstream, opt-in mathvec framework for
RV64/lp64d.  It installs the compiler/library handshake, the generated
declarations, the variant manifest machinery and the build scaffolding; the
vector implementations of log, exp, sin, cos and pow arrive with the
implementation patch that follows.  A manifest without rows exports nothing
and makes every generated header promise nothing, so the framework is inert
until a row describes an entry point.  GLIBC_2.45 is a local downstream
development symbol version; it is not a claim that any symbol is included in
an upstream glibc release.

Handshake and headers
---------------------
A caller must have RVV 1.0 and VLEN >= 128.  Vector math is advertised only
when the compiler defines __riscv_simd_math_abi_v1 == 1 and the installed
bits/riscv-mathvec.h supplies the per-function ABI mask macros generated from
mathvec-variants.mk.  The header additionally requires --enable-mathvec's
fast-math path, RV64, lp64d and RVV.  A mask records the exact fixed and
scalable, unmasked and masked variants the library promises, and
math-vector.h attaches the registered __riscv_simd_math_abi_v1(mask)
attribute to the individual __DECL_SIMD_* declarations; it does not restrict
declarations merely because a particular compile-time LMUL limit would not
generate that clone.  An ordinary compiler, or a mathvec-disabled
installation, retains scalar declarations.  A partial library is described by
clearing only the absent mask bits; in particular, missing m1 rows do not
hide installed m2 entries.  A compiler that predates the 16-bit mask receives
the historical eight-bit LMUL 1/2 subset instead of an argument it would
reject.

Mask bits, low to high, are one nibble per LMUL: m1 fixed unmasked, m1
scalable unmasked, m1 fixed masked, m1 scalable masked, then the same four
for m2, m4 and m8.  A zero function mask means the library promises no vector
entry for that function.

Variant manifest
----------------
mathvec-variants.mk is the single source of truth.  Each variant is one row
of literal make assignments naming the function, scalar, precision, arity,
lane count (x when scalable), LMUL, mode, defining routine path, exported
_ZGV symbol, symbol version, compiler capability macro, installed
availability macro, test adapter and mask kind.  Everything else is derived
from it: the exported symbols and their versions, the ABI masks, the
__DECL_SIMD_* blocks, the versioned Fortran preincludes, the per-variant
compiler flags and the generic-math test adapters.  Rows are validated
before use - an unknown function, a wrong fixed lane count, a symbol that
does not match the row, two rows resolving to the same ABI bit, and a missing
unmasked m2 pair are all hard errors.

Layout
------
This directory is the RV64/lp64d mathvec sysdeps directory, added to the
sysdeps list by riscv/rv64/rvd/Implies.  It needs a different ISA for
libmvec than for the baseline libc, and keeping the vector code in its own
sysdeps directory keeps the vector compiler flags off everything else.  The
kernels, the constant tables they include and the generic-math adapters
share the directory, the way sysdeps/aarch64/fpu keeps its vector sources,
data tables and test adapters together.  It is a sibling of riscv/rvv rather
than part of it: riscv/rvv holds the vector string and memory routines, which
are built for a vector baseline, while here only libmvec and the test
adapters use -march=rv64gcv and the baseline libc stays rv64gc.

Build-time scripts
------------------
Two generators under scripts/ are invoked by this directory's Makefile and are
part of the build, not developer tooling:

  scripts/gen-mathvec-header.py
	Writes bits/riscv-mathvec.h (availability and per-function mask macros)
	and bits/riscv-mathvec-decls.h (__DECL_SIMD_* blocks).

  scripts/gen-mathvec-fortran.py
	Writes the versioned Fortran preincludes.  It is also the manifest
	parser loaded by the other generator, so both share one contract.

The header generator re-checks the manifest on every build: the (version,
symbol) set must equal the one in Versions and libmvec.abilist, every routine
must define the symbol its row declares, and every generic-math adapter must
call it.  A manifest edited without the matching source or ABI change fails
the build instead of installing a header that disagrees with the library.
Pass --no-export-check only when running the generator by hand against a
manifest that is not part of a source tree.

Fortran preincludes
-------------------
The versioned files under finclude/ come from the same manifest.  rvv-m2-v2
promises the unmasked fixed and scalable m2 families only after it has found
the exact pair for each; rvv-m1-v3 states one directive per function with the
exact m1/m2 mask present.  A mathvec-disabled build, or a manifest without
rows, installs both with comments only, so they remain valid no-SIMD
contracts rather than falling back to a stale promise.

Loader support
--------------
sysdeps/riscv/dl-machine.h resolves marked jump slots before entering the
lazy trampoline, which does not preserve the vector calling convention, and
accounts for the processor-specific dynamic tag; tst-variant-cc,
tst-variant-cc-dlopen and tst-variant-cc-audit exercise startup, dlopen and
audit bindings.
